/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak
.DS_Store

# machine-local cargo overrides (e.g. target-dir redirect for a full C: drive
# under WSL) — not something every contributor's machine needs
/.cargo/

# precommit-audit runtime telemetry (append-only, machine-local)
.claude/audit-log.jsonl

# ephemeral session/tool state
.claude/progress.md
.compass/carve-state.json
.compass/outcomes.json
.tdd/

# agent scratch space. Deliberately INSIDE the worktree rather than under
# %TEMP%: taintguard's classifier only trusts the cwd subtree and sibling
# worktrees of the same repository, so reading a file from the harness's
# %TEMP% scratchpad taints the turn and denies every later write (CLAUDE.md
# §8, backlog 96075670).
.scratch/

# deterministic code index (rebuildable from source via `fugu-router code-index build`)
.fugu/

# Python bytecode cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# crate-local runtime progress artifacts (taskprog etc.) — never track
crates/*/.claude/

# compiled per-platform plugin binaries — NEVER committed (personal repo, no
# distribution). Local deploy builds from source: rollout/rebuild run
# `cargo build --release` and copy target/release/<name> into the live plugin
# cache. Only the platform-tagged artifacts are ignored; the hand-written
# bin/<name> wrapper dispatchers (no -os-arch tag) stay tracked.
crates/*/bin/*-darwin-arm64
crates/*/bin/*-darwin-x86_64
crates/*/bin/*-linux-arm64
crates/*/bin/*-linux-x86_64

# backlog per-project store: tasks.toml itself IS tracked (the queue ships with
# the work it describes), but its sibling lock and write-temps are runtime
# artifacts of store.rs (tasks_lock_path / save tmp) that land in the same dir.
# A committed lock would ship stale to every clone.
.backlog/*.lock
.backlog/.*.tmp.*

# specguard spec-map: a machine-local derived cache, NOT a source artifact.
# `.githooks/post-merge` runs `specguard map sync`, which writes
# `last_synced = <the merge commit that just landed>`. Tracking it therefore
# cannot converge: committing the stamp creates a new HEAD, which the next
# post-merge stamps again — measured twice in a row on 2026-08-17
# (091689e8 -> ea9c4b7e). A tracked file that is dirty after every merge
# collides with the CLAUDE.md §8 stop gate and pressures sessions toward the
# standing bypasses §5 forbids.
#
# Untracking means a fresh clone starts with NO map, so the empty-map path had
# to be checked before doing this rather than assumed. Measured 2026-08-17 with
# specguard 0.2.51 in a throwaway repo carrying only specguard.toml:
#   $ specguard audit
#   specguard audit: 0 entries mapped, 0 audit shard(s), 0 structural finding(s)
#     (map is empty — run `specguard map build` first to populate ...)
#   rc=0
# The stdout verdict does NOT collapse to clean — `main.rs:1755` guards the
# "no structural gaps" line behind `!map.is_empty()`, so absent reads as
# "map is empty", not as "audited and fine". The EXIT CODE does collapse
# (rc=0 for both empty and clean); no hook or script consumes it today
# (`.githooks/post-merge` only runs `map sync ... || true`), so this untracking
# does not arm anything, but the exit-code channel is filed as a latent
# fail-open — see the backlog entry alongside 86e0ff73.
.specguard/spec-map.toml
